  "notes": "UTC: 2026-09-14T07:18:44.665Z\nScope/result truth: preparatory test evidence only; test-green is not product DONE and does not close MASTER3178 D performance. R10's real 10s history candidate remained over deadline and R11 only removed read-time fchmod; neither is recharacterized here. No real history scan or live custody access was performed.\nChanged evidence: tests/core/task-attempt-custody-posix-adapter.test.ts:73-85,96-97,361-369,428-444,1151-1235; SHA-256 a9eec57090b1d34f6d9afbac8f17268ec11982d73a668ef7423bcbbe773c3453. FakeNative now counts every invoke and close and tracks live handles.\nActual verification: VITEST_MAX_FORKS=2 npx vitest run --configLoader runner --no-cache tests/core/task-attempt-custody-posix-adapter.test.ts; exit 0; 1 file, 55/55 tests passed. Executed repeated readFirstWriter + readVerified measurements: one-parent path = open-root 2, open-directory-at 2, identity 2, open-file-at 2, read-bounded 2, close-handle 6, total 16; four-parent path = 2, 8, 2, 2, 2, 12, total 28. The depth delta is +6 parent opens and +6 closes for the same two semantic reads. These are operation counts, not elapsed-time or an invented optimized ceiling.\nSecurity evidence: repeated reads performed zero apply-private calls; an unsafe 0600 ancestor was rejected as PRIVACY_UNVERIFIED before read-bounded; injected native identity replacement was rejected as ARTIFACT_CHANGED; successful and rejected paths ended with zero open fake handles. Existing fixture security tests all remained green.\nProducer/consumer inspection: TaskAttemptCustodyStore.readFirstWriterSnapshotUncached and readVerifiedSnapshotUncached at src/core/task-attempt-custody-store.ts:13376-13425 call the adapter independently. Adapter readFirstWriter/readVerified at src/core/task-attempt-custody-posix-adapter.ts:1390-1432 funnels each read through openFile; openParentDirectory/openDirectoryComponents at :2388-2491 reopens the bound root and every parent, performs a directory identity reread, then opens/reads/closes the file. Docker consumes repeated verified artifacts at src/orchestra/spawn-backend-docker.ts:12899,14280,14367,14392,14831,14865,14882,15158,15170,15317,15349,15692,15770,15884,15949-15963,17446,20265,20336,20366,20469,20513,20605. Production hashes inspected: adapter f89a7c880fbf464a4c301461d9933b55bcff88e1a15c21797a9a84eee36c63cf; store a0ac403cd35cb7293a59864cee86bee3b701a31cd1d1c475b8e12ca2401cc0b8.\nPrecise guarded repair recommendation: in a subsequent production-authorized task, add an operation-local read traversal scope in src/core/task-attempt-custody-posix-adapter.ts and thread its lifecycle only through src/core/task-attempt-custody-store.ts / src/core/custody-read-snapshot.ts for one bounded snapshot operation. Reuse the opened, native-pinned root/parent descriptor chain only for reads sharing the exact rootId and parent path, removing duplicate open-root/open-directory-at/close pairs within that operation; never persist it across operations, await gaps, attempts, generations, projects, tenants, or callbacks. Do not cache proof bytes as a substitute for a semantic reread. Retain OWNER_PRIVATE descriptor-relative open on every traversed component; root identity equality against the bound root; per-component returned identity/type/mode validation; the final directory identity reread; file regular-type/private-mode/single-link checks; read-bounded before/after immutable identity equality; proof equality in readVerified; and fail-closed close handling. The last verified file reread and all mount callback post-use root/project/path revalidation fences must remain. If TypeScript facade lifetime cannot express safe scoped reuse, the only permitted widening is a bounded leased-handle/batch operation across native/exec-authority/index.mjs and native/exec-authority/src/custody_posix.c with identical native identity and terminal-close semantics; no global cache or raw fd exposure.\nPlatform/tenant boundary: current executed evidence is a linux-shaped FakeNative POSIX contract only, not real Linux, macOS, or Windows performance proof. A repair must key scope by rootId + projectId + attemptId/generation and the exact parent path, and must never share across caller tenant/project authority; Windows requires its own adapter evidence and macOS/Linux require real native temporary-fixture runs before platform claims.\nMissing host-proof profile: scripts/production-wiring-host-proof-harness.mjs:19-39 and :221-257 registers closure-OS, terminal-native, memory-compact, and metrics profiles but no native-history profile (file SHA-256 26d56698a276bd20d02d4511f235f63b587bd9f12bdeb8858f291b9fab2defd0). Closure must add a new dedicated identity, for example adapterId deckent-native-custody-history-profile-v1, schemaId deckent.host-proof.native-custody-history-profile.v1, and observationGroupId deckent:native-custody-history-profile; it must bind exact built assets, host OS/arch/native ABI, tenant/project corpus digest, command/deadline, before/after operation totals, unchanged semantic result digest, security-fence outcomes, and true exit status. It must run against an isolated authorized corpus and the real native adapter, then demonstrate the owner-approved 10s history budget. It must not reuse closure-os, terminal-native-provider, memory-compact-read-export, or any unrelated profile identity.\ndocImpact: none; no product or documentation contract changed."
